Andrieux"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/37083"} "Jean-Christophe Rolland"] ". The final was not close: Redgrave and Pinsent won gold in Olympic record time, nearly five seconds ahead of Germany, who took home silver medals. Slovenia, represented by 1991 World runners-up " [:a {:href "/athletes/39677"} "Iztok Čop"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/39684"} "Denis Žvegelj"] ", took bronze, giving it one of its first Olympic rowing medals as an independent nation (the other being bronze in the men’s coxless fours)."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/37440"} "Steven Redgrave"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/37428"} "Matthew Pinsent"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/37863"} "Peter Hoeltzenbein"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/37797"} "Colin von Ettingshausen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/39677"} "Iztok Čop"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/39684"} "Denis Žvegelj"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SLO"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SLO.png"}] "SLO"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/36844"} "Michel Andrieux"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/37083"} "Jean-Christophe Roll